Modifications in this fork include:
- A-stock (China mainland) data layer using mootdx, Tencent Finance, and akshare
- Three new A-stock specific analyst agents (Policy, Hot Money, Lockup)
- A-stock trading constraints (T+1, price limits, lot sizes) in Trader and PM
- Chinese language output support
- CSI 300 benchmark for alpha calculation (replacing SPY)
- Various prompt and pipeline adaptations for A-share market specifics

See CHANGES_FROM_UPSTREAM.md for the full list of modifications.

MyTradingAgent secondary development (2026-10-04): added the FastAPI stock
query service, structured Tencent/Sina adapters, Vue stock lookup interface,
light theme, and offline contract checks. The original agent pipeline and
legacy interfaces remain inherited work. See doc/个人开发记录.md for status.

FinAgnt (2026-10-18): independently implemented Agent Loop, tool registry,
validation, bounded runtime and evidence storage. Data source endpoint, encoding
and field mapping methods adapted from the local Trading project:
backend/providers.py, backend/service.py, tradingagents/dataflows/a_stock.py,
and tradingagents/dataflows/sina_finance.py. Adapted files identify their origin.
Runtime does not import Trading or depend on its checkout path.
learn-claude-code was consulted for the loop/dispatch design; its shell tools
and agent execution code are not included in this project.

FinAgent 0.2.0 (2026-10-19): independently implemented versioned disclosure
imports, evidence-bound financial programs, calendar-aware benchmark reviews,
event timing, conversation scope, protocol-safe compaction and recovery.
Public disclosure PDFs are referenced by source manifests and are not included
in the distribution. exchange_calendars and pdfplumber remain separate optional
dependencies under their own licenses.

FinSight phase 2 (2026-10-20): independently implemented role profiles,
research coordination, SQLite task admission, evidence grants, shared budgets,
bounded expert execution, report handoffs and offline evaluation tooling.
The five-role domain split and public fund-flow / attention / news endpoint
methods were adapted from local Trading tradingagents/agents/analysts and
tradingagents/dataflows/a_stock.py. DeerFlow's harness/skill/subagent design
was consulted; no DeerFlow or LangGraph execution framework is imported.

FinSight v2.1 (2026-10-20): independently implemented versioned deliberation
contracts, host quality gates, alternating bull/bear and three-perspective
risk turns, research manager, trader proposal and portfolio decision handoffs.
Role responsibilities and direction-only research boundaries were consulted
from local Trading tradingagents/agents/researchers, managers, trader and
risk_mgmt. Runtime, contracts and prompts here are independent implementations;
no Trading/LangChain/LangGraph runtime or credentials are included.

FinSight prompt revision (2026-10-24): expanded the fourteen existing role
instructions using the local Trading tradingagents/agents/analysts,
researchers, managers, trader, risk_mgmt and quality_gate.py as references.
Adapted role methods are stored in src/finagent/skills/*/SKILL.md; shared
evidence, review and synthesis instructions retain FinAgent's native tool
contracts, scope restrictions and structured submissions. No Trading runtime
dependency was added. See doc/PROMPT_ADAPTATION.md for the mapping.

FinAgent Agent Skills migration (2026-10-24): converted role method documents
to named skill bundles with YAML discovery metadata, added lazy read-only
skill/resource tools, and separated fixed role contracts from optional methods.
The format and progressive disclosure design follow OpenAI's public Skills
documentation; the loader and execution integration are implemented locally.
PyYAML is used for safe frontmatter parsing under its separate license.
See doc/SKILLS.md for runtime behavior, packaging and validation boundaries.
